## The top station

::bg{location="funicular_top" time="morning"}
::music{action="start" mood="peaceful" volume="down"}
@narrator: The funicular car shudders the last ten metres and stops against the buffers with a sound like a dropped drawer.
@narrator: Hallen Ridge Weather Station: two stone huts, a mast, a white louvred box on legs, and more sky than you have ever been under.
@narrator{when="isSet(prev.run.route)"}: It looks exactly as you left it last summer. The door still sticks.

::use{component="enter" who="ines"}
@ines{emotion="stern"}: You're the intern. You're early. Good.
@ines{emotion="neutral"}: Ines Halvorsen. I run this place, which mostly means I write down what the sky did and apologise to it.
@player: The brochure said "a quiet summer of observation."
@ines{emotion="happy"}: The brochure is also forty years old.

## The job

::bg{location="deck" time="morning"}
::use{component="enter" who="ines" side="left"}
@ines: Readings at seven, one, and seven. Temperature, humidity, pressure, wind, cloud. You write them in the log and you do not round.
@ines: Sol keeps the radio. Nights, mostly. You'll meet him or you won't; he's a rumour until noon.
@ines{emotion="worried"}: And the village wants something from us this year.

<branch id="village" prompt="Ines taps a letter pinned by the barometer.">
  <choice id="ask" label="Ask what the village wants">
    @ines: The Lantern Festival is Sunday night. Maren wants a forecast by Friday, so they know whether to hang the lanterns or cancel.
    @ines{emotion="stern"}: A real forecast. Signed. That means you and I, with a week of your readings.
    ::accept{quest="forecast"}
  </choice>
  <choice id="shrug" label="Say you're only here for the readings">
    @ines{emotion="neutral"}: That's the job. The forecast is mine, then.
    @ines: If you change your mind, it's due Friday. The village doesn't forgive a wet festival.
    ::accept{quest="forecast"}
  </choice>
</branch>

@ines: Go and look around. The station is small. You'll run out of it by lunch.
::auto{character="ines" action="fadeOut"}
